## 4. Setup Checklists for Media Upload Integration

Here is how you would configure your frontend to load these assets for free:

### A. Integrating Cloudflare R2 for 3D/Video
Simply register a free Cloudflare account, enable **R2**, create a bucket, and upload your `.glb` model. Once uploaded, you are given a public URL. In your `constants.js` or three.js loader:

```javascript
// Example loading 3D asset from free Cloudflare R2 with zero bandwidth charges:
const PARALLETTES_3D_MODEL_URL = "https://pub-<your-unique-id>.r2.dev/models/parallettes.glb";
const HERO_VIDEO_BG_URL = "https://pub-<your-unique-id>.r2.dev/videos/hero_showcase.mp4";
```

### B. Integrating Cloudinary for Product Images
Configure your custom domain or Cloudinary cloud-name in the source code. You can upload images via their dashboard or API, and append dynamic transformation parameters in the URL:

```javascript
// Cloudinary automatically scales down, compresses, and delivers the image in Next-Gen WebP:
const productImageUrl = "https://res.cloudinary.com/yatrax/image/upload/w_800,q_auto,f_auto/v1/products/parallette_classic.jpg";
```
* `w_800` = resizes width to 800px on the fly.
* `q_auto` = automatically compresses the image to the lowest file size that still looks visually perfect.
* `f_auto` = automatically serves WebP or AVIF format if supported by the client browser.
